\ Regression: a `.module_deps` frame must not shadow the durable frame's binding for a module-less
\ quotation `call`ed while that frame is live -- checked inside a runtime-image AOT binary.
\
\ `run-stored` is a module word whose deps frame (carrying the library's `probe`, "LIB-PROBE") is
\ live while it `call`s the stored quotation. This file's own top-level `probe` returns "MAIN-PROBE".
\ The stored `[ probe ]` is module-less, so resolution runs the interpreter through jitInterpretedCall
\ under the library's live deps frame; the visibility filter must reject that foreign frame and reach
\ the durable frame's `probe`. Selective import keeps the library's `probe` out of this file's scope,
\ so the collision is purely the live deps frame against the durable frame.
use { make-holder: run-stored: } "./support/mod_deps_shadow_holder.1z" ;

probe: ( -- s ) [ "MAIN-PROBE" ] ;

[ probe ] make-holder run-stored print-line
